Package: adaptation-samsung-r7
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         adaptation-hybris-api33,
         adaptation-samsung-r7-configs (= ${binary:Version}),
         adaptation-samsung-r7-desktop (= ${binary:Version}),
         openssh-server,
Conflicts: droidian-phosh-minimal,
           droidian-minimal,
Description: Community adaptation for samsung-r7-server - metapackage
 Server/console fork of adaptation-samsung-r7 (portable-cloud-stack
 project) — no Phosh, no telephony.
 .
 Depends on adaptation-hybris-api33 (standard variant), not
 adaptation-hybris-api33-phone: the phone variant's own dependency chain
 (adaptation-hybris-phone -> ofono, ofono-scripts, ofono2mm) is how
 cellular/telephony gets pulled onto the device at all. Using the standard
 variant means that chain is never installed in the first place — this is
 a real dependency-graph exclusion, not a service masked after the fact,
 so a later `apt upgrade` can't silently bring it back.
 .
 Conflicts with droidian-phosh-minimal (and droidian-minimal, which
 currently just depends back on it in this release channel) for the same
 reason: apt's solver will refuse to have both installed, so the full
 Phosh/GNOME desktop stack this metapackage would otherwise pull in
 (phosh, gnome-control-center, chatty, evolution-data-server,
 gnome-initial-setup, etc.) never lands in the image, permanently, not as
 a one-time purge that could regress on a future apt operation.
 .
 Pulls openssh-server so a first flash always has a working SSH server. The
 base image ships no SSH server at all, which left a fresh install with no
 remote access; SSH over Wi-Fi is the dependable fallback regardless of USB
 state.

Package: adaptation-samsung-r7-configs
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         python3-gi,
         python3-evdev,
         gir1.2-gtk-4.0,
         gir1.2-adw-1,
         gir1.2-gtk4layershell-1.0,
         libgtk4-layer-shell0,
         isc-dhcp-server,
         usbmuxd,
         libpam-google-authenticator,
         oathtool,
Description: Community adaptation for samsung-r7 - adaptation configurations
 Pulls isc-dhcp-server for its dhcpd binary, invoked directly by mtp-server's
 mtp-configfs script to serve an IP over the USB RNDIS gadget (10.15.19.0/24,
 see /etc/hybris-usb/dhcpd.conf); the package's own generic
 isc-dhcp-server.service is unused and disabled in postinst.
 .
 Pulls usbmuxd so USB-connected iOS devices (e.g. tethering to an iPhone's
 Personal Hotspot) get past the default PTP-only USB configuration: usbmuxd's
 own udev rule (39-usbmuxd.rules) activates it automatically on Apple vendor
 ID match, negotiates the device into its full configuration (PTP + Apple
 Mobile Device + Apple USB Ethernet), and ipheth (built into the kernel)
 binds the Ethernet interface from there - no adaptation-side wiring needed
 beyond having the package installed.
 .
 Pulls libpam-google-authenticator + oathtool for SSH TOTP 2FA
 (key + verification code, no password auth at all — see postinst for the
 pam.d/sshd_config patches). RFC 6238 TOTP, not tied to Google despite the
 package name — no network calls, no account, works with any standards-
 compliant authenticator app.

Package: adaptation-samsung-r7-desktop
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         adaptation-samsung-r7-configs (= ${binary:Version}),
         phoc,
         waybar,
         foot,
         phosh-osk-stub,
         python3-evdev,
Description: Community adaptation for samsung-r7-server - console session
 Default (only) desktop-shell session for the r7-server fork: bare phoc
 (no phosh shell) hosting foot as its single client, over the
 hwcomposer-patched wlroots. phoc, not wayfire — see below. Used
 portrait/vertical, no auto-rotate: no iio-sensor-proxy/wlr-randr
 dependency. r7-auto-rotate.service/-script still ship inert (harmless,
 Requires=iio-sensor-proxy.service which doesn't exist in this image, so
 it simply never starts) but are no longer pulled in as a real
 dependency.
 Notes: wayfire was tried first and dropped (2026-08-11) after live
 testing found an unfixed bug — wlroots 0.18-backport surfaces (both
 xdg-shell and layer-shell) are born "uninitialized," breaking focus
 routing, so touch never reached any client. phoc doesn't have this bug
 (it's the same compositor phosh runs on this device every day, already
 proven with real touch input) and is otherwise a strictly simpler
 dependency — no window manager, no `decoration`-plugin crash to work
 around, no touch calibration matrix needed since wlroots already applies
 the output transform to absolute input devices internally (a matrix
 layered on top double-rotates touch).
